IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc3-interpretation.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46, PART II.1 Terrorism, section 83.01 (Interpretation).
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively). Written by part agent ccc3 from the text alone. Imports the keel's core (`ccc-core`).
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30).
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text. The French equivalents in
-- parentheses after a defined term are quoted inside the text lines and are not encoded.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER (the rule of 2026-10-29; assumed, not ruled by a lawyer; NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (ccc3)").
--   JUST TRUE   the facts bring the case within the term, on the text's own words.
--   JUST FALSE  the text says no in its own words ("means ... " and the case is outside; a flat negative "does not include").
--   NOTHING     not covered. A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Every JUST FALSE branch carries `-- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "<quoted words>"`; every NOTHING branch
-- carries `-- NOTHING-kind (<why>)`. Each function says in its COVERS line which rows of the text it encodes.
--
-- SEAMS. The two answers the keel's section 2 asks of this part are `s 83.01(1) the act or omission is a terrorist activity` and
-- `s 83.01(1) the group is a terrorist group` (both MAYBE BOOLEAN): the names are the ones PLAN.md section 6 gives. Paragraph (a)
-- and paragraph (b) of "terrorist activity" are separate functions, because section 7(3.74) and (3.75) (part ccc1) are written
-- over "paragraph (a)" and "paragraph (b)" of the definition. (PLAN.md also lists a seam INTO this part from section 7(3.74) and
-- (3.75); that is the other way round: those subsections read paragraphs (a) and (b) of this definition, and this definition does
-- not read them. See NOTES.md, Seams.)

§ `Section 83.01 -- Interpretation (PART II.1)`

§§ `83.01(1) Canadian`

-- COVERS: encoded | s 83.01(1) Canadian | s 83.01(1) "Canadian"
-- src:1254 | Canadian means a Canadian citizen, a permanent resident within the meaning of subsection 2(1) of the Immigration and Refugee Protection Act or a body corporate incorporated and continued under the laws of Canada or a province. (Canadien)
@ref s 83.01(1) "Canadian" (src:1254)
DECLARE `s 83.01(1) Canadian basis` IS ONE OF
    `s 83.01(1) a Canadian citizen`
    `s 83.01(1) a permanent resident within the meaning of subsection 2(1) of the Immigration and Refugee Protection Act`
    `s 83.01(1) a body corporate incorporated and continued under the laws of Canada or a province`
    `s 83.01(1) none of those`

@ref s 83.01(1) "Canadian" (src:1254)
GIVEN basis IS A `s 83.01(1) Canadian basis`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.01(1) Canadian` MEANS
    CONSIDER basis
    WHEN `s 83.01(1) a Canadian citizen` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 83.01(1) a permanent resident within the meaning of subsection 2(1) of the Immigration and Refugee Protection Act` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 83.01(1) a body corporate incorporated and continued under the laws of Canada or a province` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 83.01(1) none of those` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Canadian means"

§§ `83.01(1) entity and listed entity`

-- COVERS: encoded | s 83.01(1) entity | s 83.01(1) "entity"
-- src:1255 | entity means a person, group, trust, partnership or fund or an unincorporated association or organization. (entité)
@ref s 83.01(1) "entity" (src:1255)
DECLARE `s 83.01(1) entity kind` IS ONE OF
    `s 83.01(1) a person`
    `s 83.01(1) a group`
    `s 83.01(1) a trust`
    `s 83.01(1) a partnership`
    `s 83.01(1) a fund`
    `s 83.01(1) an unincorporated association`
    `s 83.01(1) an organization`
    `s 83.01(1) none of those kinds of thing`

@ref s 83.01(1) "entity" (src:1255)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 83.01(1) entity kind`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.01(1) entity` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 83.01(1) a person` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 83.01(1) a group` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 83.01(1) a trust` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 83.01(1) a partnership` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 83.01(1) a fund` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 83.01(1) an unincorporated association` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 83.01(1) an organization` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 83.01(1) none of those kinds of thing` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "entity means"

-- COVERS: encoded | s 83.01(1) listed entity | s 83.01(1) "listed entity"
-- src:1256 | listed entity means an entity on a list established by the Governor in Council under section 83.05. (entité inscrite)
@ref s 83.01(1) "listed entity" (src:1256)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 83.01(1) entity kind`
      `it is on a list established by the Governor in Council under section 83.05` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.01(1) listed entity` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 83.01(1) entity` kind
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `it is on a list established by the Governor in Council under section 83.05`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "listed entity means an entity on a list established by the Governor in Council under section 83.05"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "listed entity means an entity"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the thing is an entity is for s 83.01(1) "entity" and is not determined

§§ `83.01(1) terrorist activity, paragraph (a): the listed offences`

-- Paragraph (a) names ten groups of offences by the subsection of section 7 that creates them and the Convention they implement.
-- Which offence an act would be, if committed in Canada, is a fact about the act; section 7 (part ccc1) is where the offences are.
-- "committed in or outside Canada" restricts nothing: an act is within (a) wherever it is committed.
-- COVERS: encoded | s 83.01(1)(a) the act or omission, if committed in Canada, is one of the listed offences | s 83.01(1) "terrorist activity" (a)*
-- src:1258 | (a) an act or omission that is committed in or outside Canada and that, if committed in Canada, is one of the following offences:
-- src:1259 | (i) the offences referred to in subsection 7(2) that implement the Convention for the Suppression of Unlawful Seizure of Aircraft, signed at The Hague on December 16, 1970,
-- src:1260 | (ii) the offences referred to in subsection 7(2) that implement the Convention for the Suppression of Unlawful Acts against the Safety of Civil Aviation, signed at Montreal on September 23, 1971,
-- src:1261 | (iii) the offences referred to in subsection 7(3) that implement the Convention on the Prevention and Punishment of Crimes against Internationally Protected Persons, including Diplomatic Agents, adopted by the General Assembly of the United Nations on December 14, 1973,
-- src:1262 | (iv) the offences referred to in subsection 7(3.1) that implement the International Convention against the Taking of Hostages, adopted by the General Assembly of the United Nations on December 17, 1979,
-- src:1263 | (v) the offences referred to in subsection 7(2.21) that implement the Convention on the Physical Protection of Nuclear Material, done at Vienna and New York on March 3, 1980, as amended by the Amendment to the Convention on the Physical Protection of Nuclear Material, done at Vienna on July 8, 2005 and the International Convention for the Suppression of Acts of Nuclear Terrorism, done at New York on September 14, 2005,
-- src:1264 | (vi) the offences referred to in subsection 7(2) that implement the Protocol for the Suppression of Unlawful Acts of Violence at Airports Serving International Civil Aviation, supplementary to the Convention for the Suppression of Unlawful Acts against the Safety of Civil Aviation, signed at Montreal on February 24, 1988,
-- src:1265 | (vii) the offences referred to in subsection 7(2.1) that implement the Convention for the Suppression of Unlawful Acts against the Safety of Maritime Navigation, done at Rome on March 10, 1988,
-- src:1266 | (viii) the offences referred to in subsection 7(2.1) or (2.2) that implement the Protocol for the Suppression of Unlawful Acts against the Safety of Fixed Platforms Located on the Continental Shelf, done at Rome on March 10, 1988,
-- src:1267 | (ix) the offences referred to in subsection 7(3.72) that implement the International Convention for the Suppression of Terrorist Bombings, adopted by the General Assembly of the United Nations on December 15, 1997, and
-- src:1268 | (x) the offences referred to in subsection 7(3.73) that implement the International Convention for the Suppression of the Financing of Terrorism, adopted by the General Assembly of the United Nations on December 9, 1999, or
@ref s 83.01(1) "terrorist activity" (a) (src:1258-1268)
DECLARE `s 83.01(1)(a) listed offence` IS ONE OF
    `s 83.01(1)(a)(i) unlawful seizure of aircraft (subsection 7(2); Hague Convention, 1970)`
    `s 83.01(1)(a)(ii) unlawful acts against the safety of civil aviation (subsection 7(2); Montreal Convention, 1971)`
    `s 83.01(1)(a)(iii) crimes against internationally protected persons (subsection 7(3); United Nations, 1973)`
    `s 83.01(1)(a)(iv) the taking of hostages (subsection 7(3.1); United Nations, 1979)`
    `s 83.01(1)(a)(v) nuclear material and nuclear terrorism (subsection 7(2.21); Vienna and New York, 1980, as amended 2005, and New York, 2005)`
    `s 83.01(1)(a)(vi) violence at airports (subsection 7(2); Montreal Protocol, 1988)`
    `s 83.01(1)(a)(vii) safety of maritime navigation (subsection 7(2.1); Rome Convention, 1988)`
    `s 83.01(1)(a)(viii) fixed platforms on the continental shelf (subsection 7(2.1) or (2.2); Rome Protocol, 1988)`
    `s 83.01(1)(a)(ix) terrorist bombings (subsection 7(3.72); United Nations, 1997)`
    `s 83.01(1)(a)(x) financing of terrorism (subsection 7(3.73); United Nations, 1999)`
    `s 83.01(1)(a) none of the offences listed in subparagraphs (i) to (x)`

@ref s 83.01(1) "terrorist activity" (a) (src:1258-1268)
GIVEN offence IS A `s 83.01(1)(a) listed offence`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.01(1)(a) the act or omission, if committed in Canada, is one of the listed offences` MEANS
    CONSIDER offence
    WHEN `s 83.01(1)(a)(i) unlawful seizure of aircraft (subsection 7(2); Hague Convention, 1970)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 83.01(1)(a)(ii) unlawful acts against the safety of civil aviation (subsection 7(2); Montreal Convention, 1971)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 83.01(1)(a)(iii) crimes against internationally protected persons (subsection 7(3); United Nations, 1973)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 83.01(1)(a)(iv) the taking of hostages (subsection 7(3.1); United Nations, 1979)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 83.01(1)(a)(v) nuclear material and nuclear terrorism (subsection 7(2.21); Vienna and New York, 1980, as amended 2005, and New York, 2005)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 83.01(1)(a)(vi) violence at airports (subsection 7(2); Montreal Protocol, 1988)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 83.01(1)(a)(vii) safety of maritime navigation (subsection 7(2.1); Rome Convention, 1988)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 83.01(1)(a)(viii) fixed platforms on the continental shelf (subsection 7(2.1) or (2.2); Rome Protocol, 1988)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 83.01(1)(a)(ix) terrorist bombings (subsection 7(3.72); United Nations, 1997)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 83.01(1)(a)(x) financing of terrorism (subsection 7(3.73); United Nations, 1999)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 83.01(1)(a) none of the offences listed in subparagraphs (i) to (x)` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "terrorist activity means"

§§ `83.01(1) terrorist activity, paragraph (b): the purpose, the intention and the harm`

-- Paragraph (b): the act must meet BOTH of (i)(A) and (i)(B) (they are joined by "and"), and AT LEAST ONE of (ii)(A) to (E).
-- Each field is a fact a witness could state. The judgments the text turns on ("serious", "substantial", "essential service") are the
-- person's own plain answers to the question the field asks (Guide section 4: a judgment the text hands to someone else is an input).
-- COVERS: encoded | s 83.01(1)(b) the act or omission meets the purpose, intention and harm of paragraph (b) | s 83.01(1) "terrorist activity" (b)*
-- src:1269 | (b) an act or omission, in or outside Canada,
-- src:1270 | (i) that is committed
-- src:1271 | (A) in whole or in part for a political, religious or ideological purpose, objective or cause, and
-- src:1272 | (B) in whole or in part with the intention of intimidating the public, or a segment of the public, with regard to its security, including its economic security, or compelling a person, a government or a domestic or an international organization to do or to refrain from doing any act, whether the public or the person, government or organization is inside or outside Canada, and
-- src:1273 | (ii) that intentionally
-- src:1274 | (A) causes death or serious bodily harm to a person by the use of violence,
-- src:1275 | (B) endangers a person’s life,
-- src:1276 | (C) causes a serious risk to the health or safety of the public or any segment of the public,
-- src:1277 | (D) causes substantial property damage, whether to public or private property, if causing such damage is likely to result in the conduct or harm referred to in any of clauses (A) to (C), or
-- src:1278 | (E) causes serious interference with or serious disruption of an essential service, facility or system, whether public or private, other than as a result of advocacy, protest, dissent or stoppage of work that is not intended to result in the conduct or harm referred to in any of clauses (A) to (C),
@ref s 83.01(1) "terrorist activity" (b) (src:1269-1278)
DECLARE `s 83.01(1)(b) facts` HAS
    `committed in whole or in part for a political, religious or ideological purpose, objective or cause`    IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)(i)(A)
    `committed in whole or in part with the intention of intimidating the public, or a segment of the public, with regard to its security, including its economic security, or compelling a person, a government or a domestic or an international organization to do or to refrain from doing any act`   IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)(i)(B)
    `intentionally causes death or serious bodily harm to a person by the use of violence`                  IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)(ii)(A)
    `intentionally endangers a person’s life`                                                                IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)(ii)(B)
    `intentionally causes a serious risk to the health or safety of the public or any segment of the public` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)(ii)(C)
    `intentionally causes substantial property damage, whether to public or private property`               IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)(ii)(D), first condition
    `causing that damage is likely to result in the conduct or harm referred to in any of clauses (A) to (C)` IS A BOOLEAN  -- (b)(ii)(D), second condition
    `intentionally causes serious interference with or serious disruption of an essential service, facility or system, whether public or private`   IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)(ii)(E), first condition
    `the interference or disruption results from advocacy, protest, dissent or stoppage of work`            IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)(ii)(E), "other than as a result of"
    `that advocacy, protest, dissent or stoppage of work is not intended to result in the conduct or harm referred to in any of clauses (A) to (C)`   IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)(ii)(E), "that is not intended to result in"

@ref s 83.01(1) "terrorist activity" (b) (src:1269-1278)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 83.01(1)(b) facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.01(1)(b) the act or omission meets the purpose, intention and harm of paragraph (b)` MEANS
    IF     facts's `committed in whole or in part for a political, religious or ideological purpose, objective or cause`
       AND facts's `committed in whole or in part with the intention of intimidating the public, or a segment of the public, with regard to its security, including its economic security, or compelling a person, a government or a domestic or an international organization to do or to refrain from doing any act`
       AND (    facts's `intentionally causes death or serious bodily harm to a person by the use of violence`
             OR facts's `intentionally endangers a person’s life`
             OR facts's `intentionally causes a serious risk to the health or safety of the public or any segment of the public`
             OR (    facts's `intentionally causes substantial property damage, whether to public or private property`
                 AND facts's `causing that damage is likely to result in the conduct or harm referred to in any of clauses (A) to (C)`)
             OR (    facts's `intentionally causes serious interference with or serious disruption of an essential service, facility or system, whether public or private`
                 AND NOT (    facts's `the interference or disruption results from advocacy, protest, dissent or stoppage of work`
                          AND facts's `that advocacy, protest, dissent or stoppage of work is not intended to result in the conduct or harm referred to in any of clauses (A) to (C)`)))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "terrorist activity means"

§§ `83.01(1) terrorist activity: the whole definition`

-- The definition ends: "and includes a conspiracy, attempt or threat to commit any such act or omission, or being an accessory after the fact or
-- counselling in relation to any such act or omission, but, for greater certainty, does not include an act or omission that is committed during an
-- armed conflict and ... in accordance with customary international law or conventional international law applicable to the conflict, or the
-- activities undertaken by military forces of a state in the exercise of their official duties, to the extent that those activities are governed by other rules of international law."
-- COVERS: fork F-ccc3-2,F-ccc3-3 | s 83.01(1) the act or omission is a terrorist activity | s 83.01(1) "terrorist activity"; s 83.01(1) "terrorist activity" tail
-- src:1257 | terrorist activity means
-- src:1279 | and includes a conspiracy, attempt or threat to commit any such act or omission, or being an accessory after the fact or counselling in relation to any such act or omission, but, for greater certainty, does not include an act or omission that is committed during an armed conflict and that, at the time and in the place of its commission, is in accordance with customary international law or conventional international law applicable to the conflict, or the activities undertaken by military forces of a state in the exercise of their official duties, to the extent that those activities are governed by other rules of international law. (activité terroriste)
@ref s 83.01(1) "terrorist activity" (the form of the conduct, and the exclusion) (src:1257-1279)
DECLARE `s 83.01(1) form of the conduct` IS ONE OF
    `s 83.01(1) the act or omission itself`
    `s 83.01(1) a conspiracy to commit the act or omission`
    `s 83.01(1) an attempt to commit the act or omission`
    `s 83.01(1) a threat to commit the act or omission`
    `s 83.01(1) being an accessory after the fact in relation to the act or omission`
    `s 83.01(1) counselling in relation to the act or omission`
    `s 83.01(1) a form of conduct that is none of those`

-- The exclusion has two limbs, each with two conditions. "to the extent that those activities are governed by other rules of international law"
-- is a matter of degree; it is asked as the one plain fact "the activities are governed by other rules of international law" (fork F-ccc3-3).
@ref s 83.01(1) "terrorist activity" tail (src:1279)
DECLARE `s 83.01(1) exclusion facts` HAS
    `the act or omission is committed during an armed conflict`                                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `at the time and in the place of its commission it is in accordance with customary international law or conventional international law applicable to the conflict`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is an activity undertaken by military forces of a state in the exercise of their official duties`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `that activity is governed by other rules of international law`                                                IS A BOOLEAN

@ref s 83.01(1) "terrorist activity" tail (src:1279)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 83.01(1) exclusion facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 83.01(1) the armed-conflict and military exclusion applies` MEANS
        (    facts's `the act or omission is committed during an armed conflict`
         AND facts's `at the time and in the place of its commission it is in accordance with customary international law or conventional international law applicable to the conflict`)
    OR  (    facts's `it is an activity undertaken by military forces of a state in the exercise of their official duties`
         AND facts's `that activity is governed by other rules of international law`)

@ref s 83.01(1) "terrorist activity" (the whole definition) (src:1257-1279)
GIVEN form IS A `s 83.01(1) form of the conduct`
      offence IS A `s 83.01(1)(a) listed offence`
      facts IS A `s 83.01(1)(b) facts`
      exclusion IS A `s 83.01(1) exclusion facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.01(1) the act or omission is a terrorist activity` MEANS
    IF `s 83.01(1) the armed-conflict and military exclusion applies` exclusion
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not include an act or omission that is committed during an armed conflict"
    ELSE CONSIDER form
         WHEN `s 83.01(1) a form of conduct that is none of those` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "terrorist activity means"
         OTHERWISE
             IF    `s 83.01(1)(a) the act or omission, if committed in Canada, is one of the listed offences` offence EQUALS JUST TRUE
                OR `s 83.01(1)(b) the act or omission meets the purpose, intention and harm of paragraph (b)` facts EQUALS JUST TRUE
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "terrorist activity means"

§§ `83.01(1) terrorist group`

-- COVERS: fork F-ccc3-2 | s 83.01(1) the group is a terrorist group | s 83.01(1) "terrorist group"*
-- src:1280 | terrorist group means
-- src:1281 | (a) an entity that has as one of its purposes or activities facilitating or carrying out any terrorist activity, or
-- src:1282 | (b) a listed entity,
-- src:1283 | and includes an association of such entities. (groupe terroriste)
@ref s 83.01(1) "terrorist group" (src:1280-1283)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 83.01(1) entity kind`
      `one of its purposes or activities is facilitating or carrying out any terrorist activity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is on a list established by the Governor in Council under section 83.05` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an association of such entities` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.01(1) the group is a terrorist group` MEANS
    IF `it is an association of such entities`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF    (`s 83.01(1) entity` kind EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `one of its purposes or activities is facilitating or carrying out any terrorist activity`)
            OR `s 83.01(1) listed entity` kind `it is on a list established by the Governor in Council under section 83.05` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "terrorist group means"

§§ `83.01(1.1), (1.2) and (2) for greater certainty; facilitation`

-- (1.1) says what does NOT come within paragraph (b), "unless" the act meets that paragraph's own criteria. When the "unless" is met the
-- subsection says nothing more, and the answer is the paragraph's own (a fork line: F-ccc3-4).
-- COVERS: fork F-ccc3-4 | s 83.01(1.1) the expression of thought, belief or opinion comes within paragraph (b) | s 83.01(1.1)
-- src:1284 | For greater certainty
-- src:1285 | (1.1) For greater certainty, the expression of a political, religious or ideological thought, belief or opinion does not come within paragraph (b) of the definition terrorist activity in subsection (1) unless it constitutes an act or omission that satisfies the criteria of that paragraph.
@ref s 83.01(1.1) (src:1284-1285)
GIVEN `the conduct is only the expression of a political, religious or ideological thought, belief or opinion` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it constitutes an act or omission that satisfies the criteria of paragraph (b)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.01(1.1) the expression of thought, belief or opinion comes within paragraph (b)` MEANS
    IF `the conduct is only the expression of a political, religious or ideological thought, belief or opinion`
    THEN CONSIDER `it constitutes an act or omission that satisfies the criteria of paragraph (b)`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not come within paragraph (b) of the definition terrorist activity in subsection (1) unless it constitutes an act or omission that satisfies the criteria of that paragraph"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the criteria of paragraph (b) are satisfied is for s 83.01(1)(b)
    ELSE `it constitutes an act or omission that satisfies the criteria of paragraph (b)`

-- COVERS: encoded | s 83.01(1.2) a suicide bombing comes within paragraph (a) or (b) | s 83.01(1.2)
-- src:1286 | For greater certainty
-- src:1287 | (1.2) For greater certainty, a suicide bombing is an act that comes within paragraph (a) or (b) of the definition terrorist activity in subsection (1) if it satisfies the criteria of that paragraph.
@ref s 83.01(1.2) (src:1286-1287)
GIVEN `the act is a suicide bombing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it satisfies the criteria of paragraph (a)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it satisfies the criteria of paragraph (b)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.01(1.2) a suicide bombing comes within paragraph (a) or (b)` MEANS
    IF NOT `the act is a suicide bombing`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a suicide bombing is an act that"
    ELSE IF (`it satisfies the criteria of paragraph (a)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`it satisfies the criteria of paragraph (b)` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE IF (`it satisfies the criteria of paragraph (a)` EQUALS NOTHING) OR (`it satisfies the criteria of paragraph (b)` EQUALS NOTHING)
              THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the criteria of paragraph (a) or (b) are satisfied is for s 83.01(1)
              ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if it satisfies the criteria of that paragraph"

-- (2): "For the purposes of this Part, facilitation shall be construed in accordance with subsection 83.19(2)." A rule of reading that
-- points to subsection 83.19(2); it is encoded as the pass-through of that subsection's answer (the function is in `ccc3-participation`),
-- taken here as an input named for that section, which is how the keel's seams are written.
-- COVERS: encoded | s 83.01(2) facilitation is construed in accordance with subsection 83.19(2) | s 83.01(2)
-- src:1288 | Facilitation
-- src:1289 | (2) For the purposes of this Part, facilitation shall be construed in accordance with subsection 83.19(2).
@ref s 83.01(2) (src:1288-1289)
GIVEN `a terrorist activity is facilitated, by s 83.19(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.01(2) facilitation is construed in accordance with subsection 83.19(2)` MEANS `a terrorist activity is facilitated, by s 83.19(2)`
